  "metric_definition": "Share of the dataset's true rings for which the coalition flags at least one pass-through mule or collector, using the VELOCITY RULE's hard decision (ml.rule.velocity_decision over the coalition's joined view). Denominator is every ring in the dataset, including rings the coalition holds no account in.",
  "two_variants": "ring_recall is the SHIPPED rule, whose bank-spread clause (distinct_counterparty_banks >= 2) is uncomputable inside one bank -- so it fires on exactly zero accounts at N=1, and that point is the rule declining to fire, not an absence of signal. ring_recall_no_spread is the same rule with that clause dropped: the generous reading, and the honest baseline to quote a gain against. ml/rule.py reports its own single_bank variant the same way and for the same reason.",
  "not_comparable_to_claims": "docs/claims.md quotes ring recall at the XGBoost scorer's 1%-FPR operating point. This is the velocity rule's hard decision instead, which is what makes sweeping every coalition cheap. The two answer different questions and must not be read as one series.",
